&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer at Auterion, you will build software that runs on real drones. You will take Auterion’s platform into a specific customer program and make it work on their hardware, for their mission, in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a software engineering role. You will design, write, integrate and debug C++ and Python code on a Linux-based autonomy stack, working with AuterionOS, our operating system for autonomous vehicles, and Skynode, our flight and mission computer running PX4 and AuterionOS. Your work will span autonomy, computer vision, video streaming and long-range radio links, on partner platforms across aerial, maritime and ground vehicles. What sets this role apart is that your work isn’t finished when the code is merged; it’s finished when the system flies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join a forward deployed team dedicated to a single customer program, which owns the outcome from first requirement to deployed system. You will work directly with partners and customers, as well as with Auterion’s core platform, hardware and flight test teams. Between trips, you will work from our Munich office, both at your desk and on the bench.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No drone experience is required. If you have integrated software on cars, robots, industrial machines or other embedded systems, you already have the right foundation, and we will teach you the drone side.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement software for customer programs on AuterionOS and Skynode, including features, integrations, payload and sensor drivers, and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring up complete systems on real hardware, including compute, sensors, payloads and radios, and get them working end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug across the full stack, determining whether an issue stems from software, configuration, hardware or RF, and then resolving it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer mission requirements into technical solutions and working demonstrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on site with partners and customers to run flight tests, trials and demonstrations, solving problems directly in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy software releases to customer systems, including flashing, configuration and calibration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report field learnings back to core engineering in a form they can act on, and help shape the product roadmap with real customer input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document what you build so that future teams can repeat it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Computer Science, Software, Electrical, Robotics or Aerospace Engineering, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience developing software in modern C++, plus Python for tooling, automation and data analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Linux skills, including the command line, logs, Docker and networking (IP, TCP/UDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience getting software running on embedded or physical systems, including comfort with UART, CAN, I2C and SPI, wiring, and using a multimeter on the bench&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A structured approach to debugging and the ability to stay methodical under time pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication in English with customers, operators and engineers alike&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligibility for German security clearance (Sicherheitsüberprüfung)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4 or ArduPilot, MAVLink or QGroundControl&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with video pipelines, computer vision, or radio and datalink systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integration or field engineering experience in automotive, robotics or aerospace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with defense or government customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</p>

